+    "Programs based on the AutoDock software require protein and ligand to be prepared in `PDBQT` format. This file format is very similar to the PDB format but additionally stores information about the atom type and partial charges. Luckily, the [OpenBabel](http://openbabel.org/docs/index.html) package provides this functionality. First, we will retrieve a protein-ligand complex of EGFR ([2ITO](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/2ito)) from the Protein Data Bank, save the protein as PDB file and convert it to PDBQT format using OpenBabel."
